# Vulnerabilities we have reviewed and decided to accept, one ID per line.
# Every entry needs a reason, the person who accepted it, and an expiry date.
# When the date passes, Trivy reports the finding again and it must be re-reviewed.
#
# Example:
#   # Not reachable: the app never parses untrusted YAML. Accepted by Mahanth.
#   CVE-2099-0001 exp:2027-01-31

# --- Terraform: EKS cluster in the short-lived sandbox account ---

# The laptop reaches the cluster API over the internet; the sandbox gives no
# private path into the network. Accepted by Mahanth. Revisit in Phase 11.
AVD-AWS-0040 exp:2027-01-31

# The laptop's public address changes every few minutes, and the sandbox does
# not allow changing cluster settings after creation, so the allowed range
# cannot be narrowed safely. Accepted by Mahanth. Revisit in Phase 11.
AVD-AWS-0041 exp:2027-01-31

# Encrypting Kubernetes secrets needs a KMS key, and the sandbox cannot delete
# keys, so "terraform destroy" would fail. Accepted by Mahanth. Revisit in Phase 11.
AVD-AWS-0039 exp:2027-01-31
